  "ud4.1:23.1": "",
  "ud4.1:23.2": "Following variant <i lang='pi' translate='no'>anuggatā</i>. Udānavarga here has <i lang='pi' translate='no'>samudgatāṁ</i> (“arisen”), which makes for an easier reading. ",
  "ud4.1:23.3": "",
  "ud4.1:23.4": "The idiom <i lang='pi' translate='no'>hurā huraṁ</i> is literally “from here to there”. It is explained by the commentary as meaning both from one sense stimulus to the other, and from one life to the next. ",
